<%# FREE BELOW ZERO — THE SIGNAL (computed-claims spec §4). Local: `presenter` (HomePresenter).

    Split out of `_trouble` because the strip's other three arms are one element each and this one is
    a figure, a list and a pace — inlined, the `case` that dispatches the four kinds would be
    unreadable and a fifth kind would be added below the wrong `end`.

    ** THE STRIP MIRRORS THE HERO'S ARM TABLE, AND THAT IS THE FIX (fix round 1 — HIGH-1). ** This
    said "Your rules claim more than you have" on `#short?` alone — `free < 0` — which is a SIGN, and
    a sign never carries a cause. An inch above it the hero card was already splitting that same
    negative three ways on predicates that ESTABLISH one, so the two panels could contradict each
    other on the same afternoon and did, in three fixtures the answers-first review had already
    written: money walked to a savings account with no rule in existence (card: it is outside
    checking; strip: your rules claim too much), a plain overspend with nothing claimed (same), and
    claims a savings account covers in full (the give-way list naming categories whose money is
    sitting one panel further down). The arms below are `_hero.html.erb`'s, said as instructions:

      the claims outrun the money, → "Your rules claim more than you have", the give-way walk, the
      and something IS claimed        remainder if the shortfall outlasts it, the pace
      the claims outrun the money, → "You have spent past what you had". Σ claims is zero, so the
      and nothing is claimed          walk has nothing to list and does not run
      free < 0, the claims do NOT  → "Checking is short", and the money is in another account —
      outrun (the cap bound on a     which is a TRANSFER, not a rule change. Nothing is uncovered:
      negative pot)                  `unclaimed ≥ 0` IS "the user's money covers every claim"

    THE WALK IS THE PRESENTER'S (`#uncovered_claims`), not this file's, and it is gated there on the
    same `#claims_outrun_the_money?` the first two arms branch on. It takes each claim in turn until
    the shortfall is absorbed, so the LAST row is usually only PARTLY uncovered — "Car repair is
    short $120" is a different sentence from "Car repair is uncovered", and only the walk can tell
    them apart.

    THE PACE IS SAID ON EVERY ARM, deliberately: spending less for the rest of the period lands the
    figure at zero whichever way it got there, which is the one remedy §4 names that does not depend
    on which cause it was.

    ** NO FIX BUTTON, AND THE DOOR IS THE BUDGET PAGE. ** §4: "The remedy is spending less for the
    rest of the period or editing/adjusting a rule." There is nothing to move money FROM — no claim is
    money sitting anywhere — so a button offering to take $300 from Rent would be proposing an act the
    app no longer has. %>
<div class="px-6 py-3 border-b border-gray-100 last:border-b-0" data-shortfall>
  <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-4">
    <%# THE HEADLINE IS THE CAUSE, AND EVERY BRANCH IS A PRESENTER PREDICATE. A view re-deriving which
        side of the `min` won could name the wrong one of the two negatives. %>
    <span class="font-medium text-gray-900" data-shortfall-headline>
      <% if presenter.claims_outrun_the_money? %>
        <%= presenter.anything_claimed? ? "Your rules claim more than you have" : "You have spent past what you had" %>
      <% else %>
        Checking is short
      <% end %>
    </span>
    <span class="text-sm font-medium text-status-danger tabular-nums" data-shortfall-amount>
      short <%= number_to_currency(presenter.shortfall) %>
    </span>
  </div>

  <%# ** THE CAP-BOUND ARM'S OWN INSTRUCTION, AND ITS CAUSE IS ESTABLISHED BY REACHING IT. ** The
      cap's identity has two terms — `unclaimed − pot = Σ other accounts − Σ claims` — so this arm
      requires `free < 0` with `unclaimed ≥ 0`, which forces `pot < 0` and therefore
      `Σ other accounts ≥ Σ claims − pot > 0`. Another account IS holding money whenever this renders,
      which is why there is no else branch here and none on the hero's matching arm: an unreachable
      branch on a money screen is a sentence waiting to be believed.

      THE FIGURE IS `#other_accounts_total`, THE SAME SUM THE ACCOUNTS LINE PRINTS (answers-first §6),
      so the strip cannot claim money the line below it shows as absent. It names no account, because
      the total spans all of them and "it is in savings" is a guess this panel cannot make. %>
  <% unless presenter.claims_outrun_the_money? %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-700" data-shortfall-elsewhere>
      <%= number_to_currency(presenter.other_accounts_total) %> of your money is sitting outside
      checking — move some into checking to spend it.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%# THE PACE. Nil for a user who has declared no period — there is no "rest of the period" to
      spread a shortfall over — and the strip simply says one sentence fewer there. %>
  <% if pace = presenter.per_day_pace %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-700" data-shortfall-pace>
      Spending <%= number_to_currency(pace) %> a day less for the rest of this period lands it at zero.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%# WHO GIVES WAY. Reverse priority, and the figure is what THIS claim is short by after everything
      below it in the order has already given way — which is why the last row in the list is usually
      partial and says so. Empty on the two arms above that have nothing uncovered, so this renders
      nothing there rather than being gated a second way. %>
  <% if presenter.uncovered_claims.any? %>
    <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1" data-uncovered>
      <% presenter.uncovered_claims.each do |uncovered| %>
        <li class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-4 text-sm text-gray-600"
            data-uncovered-claim="<%= uncovered.category.name %>">
          <span><%= uncovered.category.name %> · <%= pool_rule_label(uncovered.line.rule) %></span>
          <span class="tabular-nums">
            <% if uncovered.whole? %>
              nothing covers its <%= number_to_currency(uncovered.claim) %>
            <% else %>
              short <%= number_to_currency(uncovered.amount) %> of <%= number_to_currency(uncovered.claim) %>
            <% end %>
          </span>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <%# ** THE PART OF THE SHORTFALL NO CLAIM ACCOUNTS FOR (fix round 1 — LOW-1). ** The walk stops
        when it runs out of claims, so a user who has spent further than their rules ever asked for
        read a headline of $900 over a list totalling $500. The list plus this line is the headline,
        by construction. %>
    <% if presenter.uncovered_remainder.positive? %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600" data-uncovered-remainder>
        …and <%= number_to_currency(presenter.uncovered_remainder) %> past everything the rules claim.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
    <%= link_to "Change a rule on the Budget page", budget_page_path, class: "text-status-info hover:underline" %>
    if this period's plan is the thing that has to give.
  </p>
</div>
